\title{Counting vs choosing}
\date{2026-05-25T20:47:47Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Note, instead of just talking about the sizes of sets we will often talk in terms of \em{choosing} elements of a set. The number of elements in a set is the same as the \em{number of ways to choose} an element of the set, so in some sense this makes no difference; but for some reason it is often helpful to think in terms of actively \em{choosing} elements rather than just passively \em{counting} them.}
